Open this address in a browser manually:
{1}

A test passkey will now be created to check whether your device can protect a KeePass database.

A page opens in the browser. Click "Continue" and choose where to save the passkey:
• this computer — the passkey manager of the browser or system (e.g. Google Password Manager in Chrome);
• a phone — scan the QR code, the passkey is saved on the phone;
• a security key (YubiKey, etc.) — insert the key and touch it.
Then confirm the passkey once more: this checks that it can produce the key for a database.

The test does not touch your databases. But the test passkey stays where you saved it: in the password list it is an entry for the site "keepass-fido2.localhost" named "KeePass: PRF diagnostics". It opens nothing and can be deleted:
• Google Password Manager — open chrome://password-manager in Chrome, search for "keepass-fido2";
• phone — its password manager (iPhone: Settings → Passwords; Android: Google Password Manager), search for "keepass-fido2";
• security key — in Chrome open chrome://settings/securityKeys → "Sign-in data", or use the manufacturer's app (Yubico Authenticator).

Continue the test?

